From 8609c09216ed5c4af4a551d01fef63471323a215 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:37:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Wallguard: DNS rewrites on its page; web.c also carries the
 audit and page fixes

- DNS rewrites, the AdGuard Home / Pi-hole feature Wallguard lacked: a table on the Wallguard
  page, a name to an address or another name, kept in the Wallguard store and written as a dnsmasq
  conf-file (shared/reaper_rewrite.h): address= / host-record= with local= so other record types
  are not forwarded, server=/*.name/# for exact names, and CNAME rows checked for duplicates and
  loops (either stops dnsmasq). One dnsmasq restart on a change, SDN instances included. Wallguard
  no longer blocks a name the router answers itself. The rewrite file is in the config backup.
- httpd/web.c also carries: the Let's Encrypt via DNS page data; blocking_request.cgi no longer
  served (the last pre-login nvram write in open code); the traffic, Wi-Fi and QoS CGIs require
  the page token; a pre-login request body is drained only up to its length; get_multifilter_info
  no longer leaks its scratch arrays (Merlin f3118f48d1); Devices folds pseudo-MLO link addresses
  into their device from the AiMesh client list whether MLO is on or off; the Connections lookup
  sorts the conntrack table once, outside the lock; the Wireless Log status as JSON.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
